/* zh-SG translations for "ch13" (generated by tools/i18n-pack.js; keys are the English source). */
Object.assign(window.I18N['zh-SG'].text, {
  "Chapter 13": "第十三章",
  "Health Class": "健康教育课",
  "Part IV — Real Life": "第四部 — 真实人生",
  "Chapter 14 — Prelims & Storm Season": "第十四章 — 预考与暴风雨季",
  "JC2, Term 2. Sexual-health week. Forty seventeen-year-olds, one school nurse, and a level of giggling that could power the MRT.": "初院二年级，第二学期。性健康周。四十个十七岁的学生、一位学校护士，以及足以给地铁供电的窃笑声。",
  "Ahem. Today I am DOCTOR Mochi. The glasses are real. The degree is from the University of Trust Me.": "咳咳。今天我是麻糬博士。眼镜是真的。学位来自“相信我大学”。",
  "ok facts. pulling out works. if she's on the pill, no STIs. first time you can't get pregnant. and you can tell if someone has something 💯": "好，冷知识。体外射精有效。她吃避孕药就不会得性病。第一次不会怀孕。而且看一眼就知道对方有没有病💯",
  "Haziq has posted four myths in one message. A personal record.": "哈齐克一条信息里塞了四个谣言。个人新纪录。",
  "Check with Dr. Mochi before anyone believes him.": "在任何人相信他之前，先向麻糬博士求证。",
  "Fact one: not having sex is the only 100% protection. Waiting is normal. Most people in this room haven't, whatever the group chat says.": "事实一：不发生性行为，是唯一100%的保护。等待是正常的。不管群里怎么说，这间教室里大部分人都还没有过。",
  "Fact two: condoms, used correctly every single time, greatly reduce the risk of pregnancy AND most STIs. Not perfectly, but a lot.": "事实二：每一次都正确使用安全套，可以大大降低怀孕和大部分性传播感染的风险。不是完美，但降低很多。",
  "Fact three: the pill prevents pregnancy, not STIs. Withdrawal is unreliable. Pregnancy can happen the very first time. And you cannot tell if someone has an STI by looking.": "事实三：避孕药能防止怀孕，但不能防止性病。体外射精并不可靠。第一次就可能怀孕。而且你不可能看外表就知道一个人有没有性病。",
  "ok that's 0 out of 4 for me. deleting.": "好吧我四题全错。删了。",
  "Repost it with a laughing emoji.": "配个大笑表情重新转发。",
  "Congratulations. Four myths now have forty readers. Myths spread faster than facts. So do STIs, when people believe myths.": "恭喜。四个谣言现在有四十个读者了。谣言传得比事实快。当人们相信谣言时，性病也传得一样快。",
  "\"I already know all this.\"": "“这些我早就知道了。”",
  "Then you will love the quiz. Everyone who \"already knows\" gets question three wrong.": "那你一定会爱上这个小测验。每个“早就知道”的人第三题都会答错。",
  "STIs. Many have no symptoms at all, so people pass them on without knowing.": "性传播感染。很多根本没有症状，所以人们在不知情的情况下就传给了别人。",
  "Untreated chlamydia or gonorrhoea can lead to infertility. Syphilis can damage the heart and brain. HIV is lifelong: very treatable now, not curable. Some types of HPV cause cancers, and there is a vaccine.": "衣原体或淋病不治疗可能导致不孕。梅毒会损害心脏和大脑。艾滋病毒（HIV）是终身的：现在已经非常可控，但无法根治。某些类型的HPV会导致癌症，而且有疫苗可以打。",
  "Whatever. There's a pill for everything.": "随便啦。什么病都有药吃。",
  "The nurse is waiting to see if anyone takes this seriously.": "护士在等，看有没有人认真对待这件事。",
  "Take it seriously. Ask how testing works.": "认真对待。问问检测是怎么进行的。",
  "Good question. Testing is confidential, quick and normal. Polyclinics, GPs and the DSC Clinic do it. I'll leave the details on the card.": "好问题。检测是保密的、很快，也很平常。综合诊疗所、家庭医生和DSC诊所都可以做。详细资料我留在卡片上。",
  "\"It'd never happen to me.\"": "“这种事不会发生在我身上。”",
  "That's what nearly everyone I've ever treated said. Then it did. Testing is free of judgement. Remember that.": "我治疗过的人几乎都这样说过。然后就发生了。检测没有任何评判。记住这一点。",
  "The anonymous question box. The nurse reads one out: \"Which kind of sex has the highest STI risk?\"": "匿名问题箱。护士念出一题：“哪一种性行为感染性病的风险最高？”",
  "Classmate": "同学",
  "Easy. Only gay guys get HIV. Hahaha.": "简单。只有同性恋男生才会得艾滋。哈哈哈。",
  "Some people laugh. Some look at the floor.": "有些人笑了。有些人低头看着地板。",
  "\"That's not true, and it's not funny.\" Then let the nurse give the real answer.": "“那不是真的，也一点都不好笑。”然后让护士给出正确答案。",
  "Thank you. The facts: unprotected anal sex carries the highest risk of HIV and many STIs, for anyone, whatever the partners' genders. Oral sex can pass on STIs too.": "谢谢你。事实是：无保护的肛交，感染艾滋病毒和多种性病的风险最高，对任何人都一样，不管伴侣是什么性别。口交也可能传播性病。",
  "Risk depends on what people do and whether they use protection. Not on who they love. And the stereotype hurts twice: it shames people, and it makes everyone else think they're safe.": "风险取决于人们做了什么、有没有采取保护措施，而不是他们爱的是谁。这种刻板印象会造成两次伤害：它羞辱了一些人，又让其他人以为自己很安全。",
  "Laugh along.": "跟着一起笑。",
  "That joke is wrong about the facts and cruel to real people. It also convinces the people laughing that they are safe. They are not, if they skip protection.": "这个玩笑不但事实错误，对真实的人也很残忍。它还让那些笑的人以为自己很安全。如果他们不做保护措施，他们并不安全。",
  "Stay quiet.": "保持沉默。",
  "The nurse corrects it herself. Nobody looks at the boy at the back who went very still.": "护士自己纠正了。没有人去看后排那个突然一动不动的男生。",
  "Peer-educator workshop. A JC2 senior hands out cards: \"Green flag or red flag?\" Your group sorts them.": "同侪教育工作坊。一位初院二年级的学长发卡片：“绿灯还是红灯？”你们组来分类。",
  "The cards: a partner who keeps pushing after a no. Wants to try choking \"because it's in videos\". Wants to film. Gets someone drunk first. Checks in and stops when asked.": "卡片上写着：被拒绝后还一直纠缠的伴侣。“因为视频里有”所以想试掐脖子。想拍下来。先把对方灌醉。会确认对方感受、被要求时就停下来。",
  "How does your group sort them?": "你们组怎么分？",
  "Only \"checks in and stops when asked\" is green. Every other card is red, whoever does it.": "只有“会确认对方感受、被要求时就停下来”是绿灯。其他每一张都是红灯，不管是谁做的。",
  "Correct. Pressure after a no is never okay. Choking or strangling can cause brain injury or death within seconds, even \"gently\", so never. Filming anyone without their free agreement is abuse.": "正确。被拒绝后还施压，永远不可以。掐脖子或勒颈在几秒内就可能造成脑损伤甚至死亡，就算是“轻轻的”也一样，所以绝对不行。没有经过对方自愿同意就拍摄，是虐待。",
  "A drunk or high person cannot consent. And checking in is not awkward. It is the green flag.": "喝醉或嗑药的人无法表示同意。而确认对方的感受一点都不尴尬，那正是绿灯。",
  "\"If they're both into it, anything goes.\"": "“只要两个人都想要，什么都可以。”",
  "\"Into it\" needs to be sober, free, and able to change its mind at any moment. Choking is never safe, no matter who agrees.": "“想要”必须是清醒的、自由的，而且随时都可以改变主意。掐脖子永远不安全，不管谁同意了。",
  "\"Videos show it, so it's normal.\"": "“视频里有，所以很正常。”",
  "Videos are made to be watched, not to be copied. They show nothing about consent, safety or how real people feel.": "视频是拍给人看的，不是给人模仿的。它们完全没有展示同意、安全，或者真实的人有什么感受。",
  "Law card, Singapore. Sexual activity with anyone under 16 is a crime, whatever they \"agree\". At 16 or 17 it is still an offence in an exploitative relationship: a teacher, coach, guardian, a big age gap or control. Consent is no defence there.": "法律卡，新加坡。与未满16岁的人发生性行为是犯罪，不管对方是否“同意”。如果对方16或17岁，在剥削性的关系中仍属违法：例如老师、教练、监护人、年龄差距大或存在控制。在这些情况下，“对方同意”不能作为辩护。",
  "Sexual messages to under-16s, and grooming, are offences. Sexual images of anyone under 16 are child abuse material. Sharing or threatening to share anyone's intimate image without consent is an offence at any age, deepfakes included. Legal is not the same as ready.": "向未满16岁的人发送性相关信息，以及诱骗（grooming），都是罪行。任何未满16岁者的性相关图片都属于儿童性虐待材料。不论年龄，未经同意分享或威胁分享任何人的私密照片都是罪行，深度伪造（deepfake）也包括在内。合法，不等于准备好了。",
  "Bro. Don't tell anyone. I have an online girlfriend. She's 24. She sends me gifts, she says my friends are immature, and she wants it to be our secret.": "兄弟。别告诉任何人。我有一个网上的女朋友。她24岁。她会送我礼物，她说我的朋友都很幼稚，她想让这成为我们的秘密。",
  "Now she wants photos. Like, private ones. That's normal right? She's mature.": "现在她想要照片。就是，私密的那种。这很正常对吧？她很成熟。",
  "Your best friend is in danger and doesn't know it.": "你最好的朋友正身处危险之中，自己却不知道。",
  "Tell him gently: this is grooming, it's not his fault, and you'll help him tell someone.": "温和地告诉他：这是诱骗，不是他的错，你会帮他告诉别人。",
  "An adult who wants a secret relationship with a teenager, sends gifts, cuts you off from friends and asks for photos? That's grooming, bro. It's not your fault. Don't send anything, don't delete the chat. Let's tell your mum, or a teacher.": "一个大人想跟一个青少年谈秘密恋爱、送礼物、让你疏远朋友、还要照片？兄弟，这就是诱骗。这不是你的错。什么都别发，聊天记录也别删。我们去告诉你妈妈，或者告诉老师。",
  "...She said nobody would understand us. That's what you're supposed to say, isn't it. If you're that kind of person.": "……她说没有人会理解我们。那种人都会这样说，对吧。",
  "Groomers can be any gender. The pattern is the same: gifts, secrets, isolation, then a request. Haziq did nothing wrong by being targeted.": "诱骗者可以是任何性别。套路都一样：礼物、秘密、孤立，然后提出要求。哈齐克被盯上，不是他做错了什么。",
  "\"Lucky you! An older woman!\"": "“你真幸运！是个姐姐！”",
  "Switch the genders and you would see it instantly. An adult targeting a seventeen-year-old in secret is not luck. It is grooming.": "把性别对调，你马上就会看出问题。一个成年人偷偷接近一个十七岁的人，不是运气，是诱骗。",
  "Help him keep the secret and take the photos.": "帮他保守秘密，还帮他拍照。",
  "BAD END #28 — Our Little Secret": "BAD END #28 — 我们的小秘密",
  "Secrets, gifts, isolation and a request for photos: that is grooming, whoever the adult is. Once the photos were sent, they became leverage. The right move was always to say it isn't his fault, keep the evidence, and tell a trusted adult or the police.": "秘密、礼物、孤立，再加上要照片：这就是诱骗，不管那个成年人是谁。照片一旦发出去，就变成了把柄。正确的做法一直都是：告诉他这不是他的错，保留证据，告诉一个信得过的大人或者报警。",
  "After the last workshop. The rooftop garden, sunset, both of you a bit embarrassed by the whole week.": "最后一场工作坊结束后。屋顶花园，日落，你们两个都因为这一整个星期而有点不好意思。",
  "On the rooftop after Health Class. {her}: \"What do we want, and when? Be honest.\"": "健康教育课后，在屋顶上。{her}：“我们想要什么？什么时候？老实说。”",
  "\"I'll be honest. And I want to hear you first, without me pushing anything.\"": "“我会老实说。我也想先听你说，我不会催你任何事。”",
  "\"There's no rush for me. And whatever we decide, either of us saying no decides it.\"": "“我一点都不急。而且不管我们决定什么，只要我们其中一个人说不，就按不来。”",
  "\"Everyone else has already. We're kind of behind.\"": "“其他人都已经有过了。我们有点落后了。”",
  "\"Ugh, that class made everything awkward. Do we have to?\"": "“唉，那堂课让一切都变得好尴尬。我们一定要谈吗？”",
  "A week later. Your flat, nobody home, a study session that stopped being about studying. The moment gets heated.": "一个星期后。你家，没人在，一场不再是在读书的读书会。气氛越来越热。",
  "You both agreed to wait.": "你们两个都说好了要等。",
  "Stop. \"Let's not. We agreed. I'll walk you home.\"": "停下来。“我们别这样。我们说好的。我送你回家。”",
  "...Yeah. Thank you. I mean it. You kept our word for both of us.": "……嗯。谢谢你。我是认真的。你替我们两个守住了约定。",
  "You walk her home. You hold hands the whole way, and that turns out to be plenty.": "你送她回家。你们一路牵着手，原来这样就已经足够了。",
  "\"Just this once.\" No talk, no plan, no protection.": "“就这一次。”不谈，不计划，不做保护措施。",
  "Wait. Stop. This isn't what we said. I want to go home.": "等等。停下。这不是我们说好的。我想回家。",
  "You stop. That part you got right. Everything before it, you'll think about for a long time.": "你停下来了。这一点你做对了。但在那之前的一切，你会想很久很久。",
  "A plan made calmly beats a decision made in a heated minute. That is the whole point of agreeing first.": "冷静时订下的计划，胜过头脑发热那一分钟做的决定。这正是事先说好的意义。",
  "\"Everyone else has already.\"": "“其他人都已经有过了。”",
  "Plenty haven't, whatever they claim. And \"everyone\" is never a reason. You two are the only people in this room.": "不管他们怎么说，还没有过的人多得是。而且“大家都这样”从来都不是理由。这个房间里只有你们两个。",
  "So. Nadia and I are kind of back together. Real one, same age, from poly. She asked: \"What do we want, and when?\" Bro, what do I SAY?": "所以。我和娜迪亚算是复合了。真的那种，同龄，理工学院的。她问：“我们想要什么？什么时候？”兄弟，我该怎么回答？",
  "Haziq wants your advice.": "哈齐克想听你的意见。",
  "\"Tell her the truth, listen to hers, and agree to wait until you're both sure. Waiting is normal.\"": "“跟她说实话，听听她的想法，约好等到你们两个都确定。等待是正常的。”",
  "Okay. And if either of us says no, that decides it. Doctor Mochi said. ...I can't believe I'm quoting a cat.": "好。还有，只要我们其中一个人说不，就按不来。麻糬博士说的。……我不敢相信我在引用一只猫的话。",
  "\"Everyone else has already. You're behind, bro.\"": "“其他人都已经有过了。你落后了，兄弟。”",
  "Most of them haven't. And \"behind\" is not a thing. Nobody is racing you.": "他们大部分都还没有。而且根本没有“落后”这回事。没有人在跟你比赛。",
  "Knowing the facts isn't permission and it isn't pressure. It's so that when you decide, in a year or in ten, you decide well.": "了解事实，不是许可，也不是压力。是为了当你做决定的时候，不管是一年后还是十年后，都能做出好的决定。",
  "And \"no\" is a full sentence. Yours too.": "而且“不”是一句完整的话。你的“不”也是。"
});
